Package: WeCoPS
Type: Package
Title: Weighting CPCA for Common and Proper Structures
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R: person("Mohamed", "Hanafi", email = "mohammed44hanafi@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Does a block weighting lead to the same interpretation as the default
    weighting in consensus principal component analysis (CPCA)? For a fixed number
    of components, the package reads the retained subspace in two bases (principal
    components; common and proper components obtained by concentration and rotation
    towards a data-driven target), measures how principal components mix common and
    proper components, applies an equivalence rule based on the motif of common and
    proper components and on their presence in the subspace of the alternative
    weighting, returns the canonical factorisation of each block on both bases, and
    draws a diagnostic sheet.
